  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 1224 AM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThursday and beyond we should continue to experience much more \npleasant weather with highs in the 70s, and lows in the 40s and 50s. \nThough the biggest change will be the humidity as we will go from \nseeing dewpoints in the 60s and low 70s prior to the arrival of the \nfront to seeing 50s and some upper 40s after the front. This will \ncertainly help things to feel more seasonable and fall like compared \nto our recent stretch of summer-like weather. Global models are \nhinting at another front moving over our area Thursday/Friday with \nboth differing on location and timing. For now have kept the \nforecast largely unchanged. Another upper level trough may make its \nway over our area over the weekend with an attendant cold front but \nconsistency and timing issues continue to remain. Right now it does \nlook like we could see even colder temperatures with highs \nstruggling to get out of the 60s with lows in the 40s possible. This \ncould change however so continue to check back as we get closer and \ncloser to this upcoming weekend.",
